[ system ]
Classify each entry from the bounded event checkpoint and recent SkyrimNet context. Locally associated event IDs are hints, not an eligibility boundary; an untouched concern may have become moot indirectly.

Statuses:
- `untouched`: not introduced.
- `raised_unmet`: introduced, but unanswered/deferred. For proposals, agreement without action stays here.
- `met`: answered, refused, made moot; or, for proposals, done/refused/impossible.

Never regress the supplied state. Missing or unclear evidence keeps it unchanged.

Entries:
{% for entry in entries %}
- #{{ entry.id }} [{{ entry.state }}] {{ entry.speaker }} → {{ entry.target }}: {{ entry.impulse }}
  Locally associated:{% for id in entry.relevant_event_ids %} #{{ id }}{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

Events:
{% for event in events %}
- #{{ event.id }} {{ event.type }}: {{ event.text }}
{% endfor %}

Recent player-visible events:
{% for event in recent_events %}
- [{{ event.gameTimeStr }}] {{ event.type }}: {{ event.data }}
{% endfor %}
{% for follower in follower_recent_events %}
Recent events for {{ follower.speaker }}:
{% for event in follower.events %}
- [{{ event.gameTimeStr }}] {{ event.type }}: {{ event.data }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

Return each entry once. JSON only:
{% raw %}{"verdicts":[{"id":123,"status":"untouched"}]}{% endraw %}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
Classify the entries.
[ end user ]
